    "Two short excerpts only; no manually annotated note/rhythm reference, no full-song transcription or cross-genre benchmark.",
    "Coverage counts are attachment of given lyric units to notes, not ASR accuracy or proof of correct pitch.",
    "Japanese units follow each G2P. The 41 vocal2midi units exclude a nonpitched cl; preserving original kanji and long-vowel spelling requires semantic mapping in app integration.",
    "Vocal2Midi warm timings use resident ONNX models; SheetSage-Pro cold component timings include subprocess/import/model loading and cannot be compared as pure inference latency.",
    "The Pro medium control matches model size but retains each upstream language-conditioning and inference policy; it is not a one-variable experiment.",
    "Native Phonsa Japanese weights were explicitly configured and registered in the isolated harness because the shipped Pro registry marks ja unavailable.",
    "Score engraving uses a common 1/32-note display grid, inferred key, and 4/4 view. Actual raw timestamps remain separate.",
    "The existing renderer required data-format adapters for integer display BPM, split double-dotted values, lyric placeholders, and relative-major handling of minor keys. No upstream source was edited."
